Haiku ext4 filesystem driver
===========================

This branch introduces a dedicated ext4 filesystem handler.

Phase 1 intentionally shares the proven ext2 implementation for vnode,
directory, extent, allocation and journal plumbing while adding an explicit
ext4 feature-negotiation boundary.  It is not advertised as full Linux-ext4
feature parity yet.

Supported target:
  - extents
  - 64-bit block addressing as represented by the current Haiku structures
  - flex_bg
  - directory indexing
  - metadata checksum infrastructure already present in the Haiku driver
  - extra inode size/timestamps
  - large files

Explicitly rejected:
  - bigalloc
  - meta_bg
  - MMP
  - inline_data
  - EA_INODE
  - encrypt
  - casefold
  - largedir
  - external journal device
  - quota/project/verity features
  - fast commit

The implementation will be migrated from the ext2-derived translation units
in subsequent phases so that ext4-specific invariants can be enforced at the
filesystem boundary rather than through the old ext2 feature masks.
